Independent physical-theta to count-lambda derivation
====================================================
Let X be centered, variance one, with p=P(X>0), q=1-p, v=pq>0,
and m=EX_+=EX_->0. Assign zeros to B=0. Conditional means are -m/q
and m/p. Put ell=m/v and U=X/ell-(B-p). Then E(U|B)=0, so writing
s=qE(U²|B=0)+pE(U²|B=1) gives 1=ell²(v+s). The physical within-sign
variance is theta=ell²s. Therefore

 theta=s/(v+s), m²=v²/(v+s), lambda=n*s=n*v*theta/(1-theta).

These are exact identities, including theta=0 and atoms at zero. Bounded
support is unnecessary for this second-moment identity. The resource's raw
row theta has this physical meaning: source_round rounds it upward;
retained_cell preserves/intersects physical bounds; amplitude uses
ell>=sqrt((1-theta_upper)/vmax); the harmonic step converts an actual lambda
bound to theta<=lambda/(n*vmin+lambda). In the actual count kernel,
exact35_core sets s in [lo/n,hi/n] and h=sqrt(v+s). Thus the count interval
coordinate is exactly lambda=n*s; it is not n*theta.

On any closed 0<l<=p<=u<1, define
vmax=1/4 if l<=1/2<=u, otherwise max(l(1-l),u(1-u)). If the same law has
0<=theta<=T<1, monotonicity in v and theta gives the rational cap

                    lambda <= n*vmax*T/(1-T).

Intersection of the incoming lambda interval with this upper bound is a
necessary-condition contraction. Reject only when lo>new_hi; preserve an
equal endpoint. A theta value from a FLOAT exploration is not an acquired
premise. The bound must come from the accepted same-law resource or be
assumed explicitly in a conditional count contract, then acquired later.

The final resource export copies the earlier row.lambda_max while the last
geometry step may further decrease row.theta. Thus the exported scalar
lambda_max can be a weaker upper bound than this new cap, without either
being incorrect. The cap may be substantially useful in count leaves.

A direct alternative is already stored in each successful resource history:
with actual conditional supports U0 in[-A0,a0], U1 in[-a1,A1], one has
EUi²<=Ai*ai and lambda<=n*Amax*max(p,q)*(a0+a1). Intersecting this with
the existing simultaneous relation d/d0+lambda/Lambda<=1 yields

        lambda <= L=(1/Lambda+1/(n*Amax*max(u,1-l)*d0))^-1.

The exact field lambda_geometry_cap is this L. Every accepted history step
retains the same law, so all stored caps may be intersected. This avoids the
small loss introduced by converting L to theta using vmin then back using
vmax. Scope and exact field provenance still require a final interface.

