In exact35_core, cfg.Lambda enters not just the rootbox but also
 d <= d0*(1-lambda/cfg.Lambda).
Replacing that denominator by a new independent upper cap is invalid.
For example d0=Lambda=1, actual d=lambda=1/2 satisfies the old joint plane
and the extra lambda<=3/5, but violates d+lambda/(3/5)<=1. Keeping the old
noise price alone does not fix this. Add a separate acquired_theta or
